WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.128 --> 00:00:02.777
- We used to go to topless bars.

00:00:02.777 --> 00:00:04.444
Strip shows.
- What?

00:00:05.559 --> 00:00:06.642
I had no idea

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:09.407
that you used to do that.

00:00:09.407 --> 00:00:10.905
- I was fun, I liked it.

00:00:10.905 --> 00:00:11.897
- Fatherhood!

00:00:11.897 --> 00:00:14.049
It's Father's Day, comin' up soon.

00:00:14.049 --> 00:00:15.229
- [Zach] About two years ago, the Try Guys

00:00:15.229 --> 00:00:17.346
made a motherhood series for mother's day.

00:00:17.346 --> 00:00:18.736
- [Keith] So we're doing
a whole fatherhood series.

00:00:18.736 --> 00:00:21.858
- One video every day
that's all about dads.

00:00:21.858 --> 00:00:25.232
(crying)
- Uh oh.

00:00:25.232 --> 00:00:26.863
- Is it rude for me to
say that I want out?

00:00:26.863 --> 00:00:30.746
- The Try Guys are
going to become fathers.

00:00:30.746 --> 00:00:33.317
We're gonna become daddies.

00:00:33.317 --> 00:00:35.106
Or at least invite our dads to come in

00:00:35.106 --> 00:00:36.705
from across the nation to let us know

00:00:36.705 --> 00:00:39.372
how terrible it was to raise us.

00:00:40.214 --> 00:00:42.797
(upbeat music)

00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:55.898
- So today we're recreating
photos of our dads.

00:00:55.898 --> 00:00:57.848
- In an aim to better
understand who they were

00:00:57.848 --> 00:00:58.681
when they were our age.

00:00:58.681 --> 00:01:01.413
- I think many times, the
father/son relationship

00:01:01.413 --> 00:01:03.126
is the least developed in the family.

00:01:03.126 --> 00:01:05.280
- His life starts when I was born.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:07.967
- But before that he's just like us?

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:09.944
- I don't really know a ton about my dad,

00:01:09.944 --> 00:01:11.479
which is why we wanted
to do this whole series.

00:01:11.479 --> 00:01:13.312
- Let's get daddy-ied.

00:01:14.179 --> 00:01:15.012
Daddies.

00:01:16.315 --> 00:01:17.148
- It's weird.

00:01:17.148 --> 00:01:18.054
There some photos I look at my dad

00:01:18.054 --> 00:01:19.877
and I'm like, "I don't
recognize that man."

00:01:19.877 --> 00:01:20.934
And there's some photos I'm like,

00:01:20.934 --> 00:01:22.491
"Wow, that's my face."

00:01:22.491 --> 00:01:24.587
I doubt he knows what
day this photo was taken,

00:01:24.587 --> 00:01:28.006
but my dad is rockin' a mean porn-'stache.

00:01:28.006 --> 00:01:29.903
Is it weird to call your
dad's 'stache a porn-'stache?

00:01:29.903 --> 00:01:31.127
It's a porn-'stache.

00:01:31.127 --> 00:01:33.904
I think my dad and I are really
similar in a lot of ways.

00:01:33.904 --> 00:01:35.385
My dad and I talk about music

00:01:35.385 --> 00:01:38.460
and we talk about football
and that's kinda it.

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:40.529
When I check in with my parents about how

00:01:40.529 --> 00:01:42.389
my life is going, I call my mom.

00:01:42.389 --> 00:01:44.328
I wanna get advice from him,

00:01:44.328 --> 00:01:45.316
and we don't do that.

00:01:45.316 --> 00:01:48.262
I know my mom always says
that my dad was funny.

00:01:48.262 --> 00:01:49.438
I don't see it.

00:01:49.438 --> 00:01:51.574
Apparently that's how my dad won my mom

00:01:51.574 --> 00:01:52.906
and god knows if I find somebody

00:01:52.906 --> 00:01:54.371
that's gonna be how I do it.

00:01:54.371 --> 00:01:56.402
- A lot of my memories are
playing outside with my dad.

00:01:56.402 --> 00:01:58.289
So my dad is a doctor, but he kind of

00:01:58.289 --> 00:02:00.512
took some time to figure that out.

00:02:00.512 --> 00:02:02.956
He was actually a tennis pro for a while.

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:05.121
I always think of my
dad as a clean cut guy.

00:02:05.121 --> 00:02:06.619
His hair is long.

00:02:06.619 --> 00:02:08.428
My dad has never had long hair.

00:02:08.428 --> 00:02:11.547
I definitely got my
competitive nature from my dad.

00:02:11.547 --> 00:02:13.185
We would play a lot of sports growing up

00:02:13.185 --> 00:02:15.449
and he would always beat me.

00:02:15.449 --> 00:02:18.227
My dad would play the
sports that he was good at.

00:02:18.227 --> 00:02:20.107
We would play tennis,
we would play squash,

00:02:20.107 --> 00:02:21.457
we would play ping pong.

00:02:21.457 --> 00:02:24.252
We never really played soccer.

00:02:24.252 --> 00:02:25.137
Hm.

00:02:25.137 --> 00:02:27.323
- I love my dad, he's
great, he's a big old nerd.

00:02:27.323 --> 00:02:28.939
'Cause when people always
talked about how tall I was,

00:02:28.939 --> 00:02:31.273
he'd say, "Yeah, he's grew-some."

00:02:31.273 --> 00:02:32.608
You think your dad loves puns?

00:02:32.608 --> 00:02:33.792
My dad invented puns.

00:02:33.792 --> 00:02:36.968
I don't know a ton about
my dad's life before me.

00:02:36.968 --> 00:02:39.632
The only thing I know is
that he is a mining engineer

00:02:39.632 --> 00:02:41.391
and he was in a barbershop quartet called

00:02:41.391 --> 00:02:43.173
the Four-Ever Yours.

00:02:43.173 --> 00:02:45.919
(rimshot drumming)
I mean come on.

00:02:45.919 --> 00:02:47.671
Music is really one of the biggest ways

00:02:47.671 --> 00:02:49.936
that I think my dad and I have bonded.

00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:51.773
So I thought if I was gonna
make anything of my dad,

00:02:51.773 --> 00:02:54.400
I should make his iconic foursome

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:56.054
with my iconic foursome.

00:02:56.054 --> 00:02:59.784
- How different the Try Guys
could've been, you know.

00:02:59.784 --> 00:03:02.353
- When I was a kid, I really hated my dad.

00:03:02.353 --> 00:03:04.239
He was never home.

00:03:04.239 --> 00:03:06.254
He had to work about two hours away

00:03:06.254 --> 00:03:07.601
so for a chunk of my childhood,

00:03:07.601 --> 00:03:09.631
he was never there for five days a week.

00:03:09.631 --> 00:03:11.169
Every time I saw my dad, he had to play

00:03:11.169 --> 00:03:12.697
the disciplinarian role.

00:03:12.697 --> 00:03:14.230
In retrospect, I feel really bad for him

00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:16.679
because we did have a
lot of issues growing up

00:03:16.679 --> 00:03:18.944
but I think a lot of it was just

00:03:18.944 --> 00:03:21.955
the expectation of what a
man should be in his family.

00:03:21.955 --> 00:03:23.632
And then my parents got divorced.

00:03:23.632 --> 00:03:27.114
My dad versus Jae are
two different people.

00:03:27.114 --> 00:03:29.125
Jae is the man that
came out of the divorce.

00:03:29.125 --> 00:03:31.262
He became everything that I think

00:03:31.262 --> 00:03:34.292
he was destined to be,
which is a good person

00:03:34.292 --> 00:03:36.518
with a great sense of humor.

00:03:36.518 --> 00:03:39.116
I'm very excited to learn
what this moment was

00:03:39.116 --> 00:03:40.451
in this hammock where he's like,

00:03:40.451 --> 00:03:42.436
dreamily looking up at that sky

00:03:42.436 --> 00:03:44.366
that would warrant that smile.

00:03:44.366 --> 00:03:45.199
When I was a child, I would never

00:03:45.199 --> 00:03:46.796
see that expression on his face.

00:03:46.796 --> 00:03:50.546
♫ Daddy, daddy, daddy, daddy

00:03:53.587 --> 00:03:55.988
- So just be like, "Hey Adam."

00:03:55.988 --> 00:03:57.169
Yeah, call me Adam.

00:03:57.169 --> 00:04:01.999
- I'm Adam Kornfeld and I
am Zach Kornfeld's father.

00:04:01.999 --> 00:04:02.832
Hi Zach.

00:04:02.832 --> 00:04:05.367
I wanted to be in the music
business since I could remember.

00:04:05.367 --> 00:04:07.126
I was eight or nine years old.

00:04:07.126 --> 00:04:10.232
I used to listen to Casey
Kasem's American Top 40

00:04:10.232 --> 00:04:11.065
and I was hooked.

00:04:11.065 --> 00:04:12.246
- He loves rock n' roll.

00:04:12.246 --> 00:04:13.672
I remember listening to the Beach Boys

00:04:13.672 --> 00:04:15.456
and the Beatles and Bob Marley.

00:04:15.456 --> 00:04:18.503
- I look like Freddie
Mercury's pudgier brother.

00:04:18.503 --> 00:04:19.868
- I'm about the same age as you are now

00:04:19.868 --> 00:04:20.774
in that photo.

00:04:20.774 --> 00:04:23.962
I was on the beach on Fire Island.

00:04:23.962 --> 00:04:26.014
One of my favorite places in the world.

00:04:26.014 --> 00:04:27.624
Your grandparents actually met there

00:04:27.624 --> 00:04:29.301
in the last 1950s.

00:04:29.301 --> 00:04:30.874
That's a happy memory photo.

00:04:30.874 --> 00:04:32.957
- I'm Jim, I'm Ned's dad.

00:04:33.980 --> 00:04:38.340
And, then I don't know what
I'm talking about after that.

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:39.447
(laughing)

00:04:39.447 --> 00:04:41.701
I've played practically every sport.

00:04:41.701 --> 00:04:43.063
It's not as popular nowadays,

00:04:43.063 --> 00:04:45.250
but in the 70s, tennis was huge.

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:47.239
- God, it's such an action shot.

00:04:47.239 --> 00:04:48.829
We're like, jumping out at this.

00:04:48.829 --> 00:04:50.861
We sometimes joke that I'm
really obsessed with marriage

00:04:50.861 --> 00:04:52.870
but I think I get it from my dad.

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:55.406
He will do anything for his family.

00:04:55.406 --> 00:04:56.933
- Every summer, in fact, I've never missed

00:04:56.933 --> 00:04:59.783
a summer in my life,
with my dad and my mom,

00:04:59.783 --> 00:05:02.753
we go to this place called
the Thousand Islands.

00:05:02.753 --> 00:05:05.564
Crowds would come out to
watch these tournaments

00:05:05.564 --> 00:05:06.397
that we'd have.

00:05:06.397 --> 00:05:09.162
This photo is of me in
one of the tournaments.

00:05:09.162 --> 00:05:11.026
(grunting)

00:05:11.026 --> 00:05:12.472
- To the left.

00:05:12.472 --> 00:05:14.624
You know, even just recreating
this in a photo studio

00:05:14.624 --> 00:05:15.590
is tough.

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:16.455
I don't think I fully realized

00:05:16.455 --> 00:05:18.096
how good at tennis my dad was.

00:05:18.096 --> 00:05:20.583
- I know this smile of my dad's very well.

00:05:20.583 --> 00:05:21.639
He has one smile.

00:05:21.639 --> 00:05:24.478
- I'm Don Habersberger,
I'm Keith's father,

00:05:24.478 --> 00:05:26.645
and he has two other sons.

00:05:28.232 --> 00:05:29.065
Did I say that?

00:05:29.065 --> 00:05:30.049
Let's start that all over.

00:05:30.049 --> 00:05:32.162
I'm recently retired and I spent

00:05:32.162 --> 00:05:34.688
over 40 years in the mining industry.

00:05:34.688 --> 00:05:37.073
I was in choirs ever since fourth grade.

00:05:37.073 --> 00:05:39.330
I began going to barbershop practices

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:42.997
and got into a quartet,
the Four-Ever Yours.

00:05:44.136 --> 00:05:45.589
(rimshot drumming)
It's sort of a play on words.

00:05:45.589 --> 00:05:49.172
Music was the part to
balance my life with.

00:05:50.066 --> 00:05:52.733
♫ Sweet Adeline

00:05:54.130 --> 00:05:56.797
♫ Sweet Adeline

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:01.922
- I'm Eugene's dad.

00:06:01.922 --> 00:06:04.922
I was 41 years old when he was born.

00:06:06.137 --> 00:06:07.408
Kinda old.

00:06:07.408 --> 00:06:08.866
- I guess he's relaxed
now 'cause he's retired

00:06:08.866 --> 00:06:10.688
but he had a pretty stressful life.

00:06:10.688 --> 00:06:11.931
Even in this photo, I have no idea

00:06:11.931 --> 00:06:13.251
if this was taken in Korea.

00:06:13.251 --> 00:06:15.019
Growing up in a war torn country, I think,

00:06:15.019 --> 00:06:15.996
does something to you.

00:06:15.996 --> 00:06:18.040
- I kinda used to be dreamer.

00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:20.640
All I was thinking about
was like a John Wayne

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:23.903
and cowboys, that's
all I was into, movies.

00:06:23.903 --> 00:06:27.640
It wasn't like that
when I came to the U.S.

00:06:27.640 --> 00:06:29.776
It's a very conservative country,

00:06:29.776 --> 00:06:33.191
you have to work very
hard trying to make money.

00:06:33.191 --> 00:06:34.925
Trying to support the family.

00:06:34.925 --> 00:06:38.048
- For an asian family, and
for an immigrant family,

00:06:38.048 --> 00:06:40.087
we don't share stories to begin with.

00:06:40.087 --> 00:06:41.362
So to force my dad to come here

00:06:41.362 --> 00:06:43.232
and talk about that stuff on screen

00:06:43.232 --> 00:06:45.688
is pretty uncomfortable for both of us.

00:06:45.688 --> 00:06:48.855
He seemed happier before he was a dad.

00:06:51.702 --> 00:06:53.119
- I was so happy.

00:06:57.110 --> 00:06:57.943
- [Zach] Hey dad.

00:06:57.943 --> 00:06:59.119
- Hey Zach.
- How are you?

00:06:59.119 --> 00:06:59.952
- I'm great.

00:06:59.952 --> 00:07:00.868
- [Ned] Welcome to Buzzfeed.

00:07:00.868 --> 00:07:01.701
- [Jim] Thanks.

00:07:01.701 --> 00:07:03.118
- [Ned] This is where I work.

00:07:03.118 --> 00:07:04.955
- Wow.
- Yeah, wow.

00:07:04.955 --> 00:07:07.393
- Great shirt choice.
- I like yours, too.

00:07:07.393 --> 00:07:08.948
- What would your normally
be doing right now?

00:07:08.948 --> 00:07:09.781
- Playing golf.

00:07:09.781 --> 00:07:11.782
- I don't really know about you in between

00:07:11.782 --> 00:07:14.231
college and my birth.

00:07:14.231 --> 00:07:16.989
The in between is like
really foggy and hazy.

00:07:16.989 --> 00:07:19.479
- Yeah for me, too.
- (laughing) Yeah, I bet.

00:07:19.479 --> 00:07:21.863
Show us that photo.

00:07:21.863 --> 00:07:24.113
(laughing)

00:07:25.853 --> 00:07:28.534
We got the same belly,
same chest hair pattern.

00:07:28.534 --> 00:07:30.205
- So handsome.

00:07:30.205 --> 00:07:31.541
- You're just saying that
'cause I look like you

00:07:31.541 --> 00:07:32.610
in this photo.

00:07:32.610 --> 00:07:33.443
- Yeah.

00:07:33.443 --> 00:07:35.042
- [Zach] I have bigger nipples than you.

00:07:35.042 --> 00:07:37.039
- Yes, bigger than most people.

00:07:37.039 --> 00:07:39.209
I was probably listening
to Bruce in that picture.

00:07:39.209 --> 00:07:40.042
- I should've known.

00:07:40.042 --> 00:07:41.763
You are an east coast dad.
- Yes.

00:07:41.763 --> 00:07:44.353
♫ Baby we were born to sit

00:07:44.353 --> 00:07:46.331
- You and mom are both
like crazy workaholics.

00:07:46.331 --> 00:07:47.953
I think that's why you
love the beach so much

00:07:47.953 --> 00:07:49.478
'cause this is just like the only place

00:07:49.478 --> 00:07:51.603
that you turn your brain off.

00:07:51.603 --> 00:07:52.436
- That's true.

00:07:52.436 --> 00:07:54.946
This is my weekend relaxation moment.

00:07:54.946 --> 00:07:57.371
Your job, like my job, it's your life.

00:07:57.371 --> 00:07:58.204
- Yeah.

00:07:58.204 --> 00:07:59.864
- Sons being similar to their fathers.

00:07:59.864 --> 00:08:01.466
- It's horrifying.
(laughing)

00:08:01.466 --> 00:08:05.588
- Okay, let's see it.
(laughing)

00:08:05.588 --> 00:08:06.813
- That's a good likeness.

00:08:06.813 --> 00:08:08.141
That's a nice wig you got there.

00:08:08.141 --> 00:08:08.974
- [Ned] Thank you.

00:08:08.974 --> 00:08:09.807
- [Jim] Where'd you get the racquet?

00:08:09.807 --> 00:08:11.288
I don't have those racquets anymore.

00:08:11.288 --> 00:08:13.766
- Ariel had a racquet that she picked up

00:08:13.766 --> 00:08:14.963
at a flea market.

00:08:14.963 --> 00:08:16.548
- So this is during a tournament.

00:08:16.548 --> 00:08:17.381
- Oh, a tournament?

00:08:17.381 --> 00:08:20.251
This photo suddenly has
stakes that I didn't realize.

00:08:20.251 --> 00:08:21.084
- Yeah

00:08:21.084 --> 00:08:22.165
- Were you the reigning champion?

00:08:22.165 --> 00:08:23.555
- Yeah.
- Wow.

00:08:23.555 --> 00:08:25.297
So is that something the impressed mom?

00:08:25.297 --> 00:08:27.333
- No, she isn't impressed
by that kind of stuff.

00:08:27.333 --> 00:08:28.846
That's what I looked
like when I dated her.

00:08:28.846 --> 00:08:31.477
- Oh.
(laughing)

00:08:31.477 --> 00:08:32.394
She was into that.

00:08:32.394 --> 00:08:34.198
- [Jim] What was her deal anyway?

00:08:34.198 --> 00:08:35.254
I was very immature.

00:08:35.254 --> 00:08:36.087
- [Ned] How so?

00:08:36.087 --> 00:08:37.166
- I did some pranks.

00:08:37.166 --> 00:08:39.558
I would get really frustrated easily.

00:08:39.558 --> 00:08:40.889
As I've gotten older, I've gotten

00:08:40.889 --> 00:08:42.292
more wise than I used to be.

00:08:42.292 --> 00:08:43.981
- Hm, interesting.

00:08:43.981 --> 00:08:47.393
I'm about to turn 30, y'all.
(laughing)

00:08:47.393 --> 00:08:48.226
- Looking at the original photo,

00:08:48.226 --> 00:08:50.454
I already look pretty similar.

00:08:50.454 --> 00:08:52.287
